ssure and allowing work extraction by expansion to the initial pressure. A particular type of pressure gain combustion (PGC) device is described, which is under investigation at GRC (Glenn Research Center). The Resonant Pulse Combustor (RPC) has been largely overlooked due to its theoretically low performance. However, its practical performance is quite competitive with other PGC systems, and its physical simplicity is unmatched.","isLessonsLearned":false,"disseminated":"DOCUMENT_AND_METADATA","meetings":[{"country":"Germany","submissionId":20180006753,"endDate":"2018-09-21T00:00:00.0000000+00:00","sponsors":[{"organizationId":"9ff5dedf3df55c348e407bb9e5e0541d","meta":{"organization":{"name":"Technische Univ.","location":"Berlin, Germany"}},"meetingId":"73e57e66e4aa48f1a9918edbca1b8072","id":"f2355ff92120486bb8f3aa733d4272a4"},{"organizationId":"e0f9cccb96e44011966d99ef23181b77","meta":{"organization":{"name":"Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft","location":"Bonn, Germany"}},"meetingId":"73e57e66e4aa48f1a9918edbca1b8072","id":"41882523afed425cbcf19dcf6e540203"}],"name":"Active Flow and Combustion Control (AFCC 2018)","location":"Berlin","id":"73e57e66e4aa48f1a9918edbca1b8072","startDate":"2018-09-19T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"publications":[{"submissionId":20180006753,"id":"f275a657024c4cf8bb40f84fda8bdd49","publicationDate":"2018-09-19T00:00:00.0000000+00:00"}],"status":"CURATED","related":[],"downloads":[{"draft":false,"mimetype":"application/pdf","name":"20180006753.pdf","type":"STI","links":{"original":"/api/citations/20180006753/downloads/20180006753.pdf","pdf":"/api/citations/20180006753/downloads/20180006753.pdf","fulltext":"/api/citations/20180006753/downloads/20180006753.txt"}}],"downloadsAvailable":true,"index":"submissions-2026-10-08-04-13"}